const prompt=`Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: Scrapkeep initial visual-direction candidate A, one landscape gameplay-camera concept, 16:9.
Primary request: Show a playable-looking stylized 3D scene in a weathered Southwest river gorge, demonstrating tactile workshop-built machines and a society designed for rolling gyroscopic balls. A coherent, achievable game-art target, not a photograph or cinematic poster.
Composition: close third-person chase view behind and slightly above the player, 4 m camera height. The entire player sphere sits in the lower left third, about one quarter of image height; the action and an open escape route are clearly visible ahead. Broad concave stone travel bank curves right around an ancient reactor Warden in the middle-right. The Warden has its own circular hostile floor telegraph. Leave a wide clean lane outside that circle on the left. A river and green riparian plants run deep below on the far left. A colossal ancient dam and three weathered tower silhouettes anchor the far center. Distant blue mountain layers and open sky. Show banked paths and one functional launch chute integrated into masonry on the far right. No cars, wheel chassis or flat arena room.
Player: a fox pilot visibly seated upright INSIDE a fully enclosing clear spherical pressure-glass hull. The true round ball contacts the ground. A visible repaired inner gimbal cradle supports the pilot. One worn copper-and-painted-metal gyroscopic orbit ring encircles the ball near its equator with clearance above ground. Mint coil light only at the intake under the pilot and tiny working ring pips. A few bolted repair plates and hose clamps show salvage ingenuity, but glass stays clear enough to read fox ears, orange fur, cream cheek profile, dark work cap and gloved hands. All limbs remain inside the sphere. No exposed cockpit, separate head bubble, wheels, glossy toy shell, decorative neon or multiple balls.
Boss: a heavy non-humanoid cast-metal ancient reactor machine, approximately three player-sphere diameters tall, leaning forward with a scarred containment dome, an eye-like narrow blue crack, three broad vent stacks and thick asymmetric clamp jaws visibly clutching a central beacon mast. Dull petrol enamel and cast iron, blue light restricted to dark recessed cracks. Its silhouette communicates a pulse mechanism preparing to fire, not a decorative fountain. No bolts used as the ancient machine's dominant construction vocabulary. It stays completely separate from the player.
Threat: exactly one unbroken CIRCULAR ground footprint around the boss, drawn flush on the terrain with red-orange and charcoal diagonal striping. The player is wholly outside it. No red-orange glow on the player, no mint glow on the boss, no decorative hazard tape elsewhere. Clean open escape ground.
Treatment A: tactile stylized 3D, bold rounded-but-angular manufactured forms, broad bevels, restrained hand-authored wear, deliberate large material patches. Convincing matte sandstone, worn painted metal, copper, rubber, dirty joints and clear glass are visibly different. Wear has a cause, not uniform noise. Material richness lives in roughness and a few broad scratches; no microscopic greebles. Strong but soft-edged directional Southwest afternoon sun with cool broad sky fill. Deep, readable shadows rather than black voids; atmospheric depth. Natural greenery and blue distance break up warm stone. Dynamic, adventurous, scrappy and inviting.
Palette: sandstone #c6a274, rust #9b513a, charcoal #242a28, dull petrol #365754, bone #d2c5a5, copper #b77843. Concentrated field mint #8bf0d3 belongs to the player's working coils. Boss cracks are narrow blue #3d8bff. Danger footprint is #ff5a3c and charcoal.
Constraints: no text, labels, logos, watermark, HUD or invented UI. No depth-of-field blur, motion blur, film grain, lens flare or overwhelming particles. Keep the composition readable as a real gameplay scene. This is a concept reference, not a screenshot.`;
store("prompt_a",prompt);
const out="/tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development/sketches/core-loop/design-v2/visual-development";
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: "+out+"/prompt-a.txt\n+"+prompt.split("\n").join("\n+")+"\n*** End Patch"));
// @exec: {"yield_time_ms": 120000, "max_output_tokens": 600}
const result=await tools.image_gen__imagegen({prompt:load("prompt_a")});store("image_a_result",result);generatedImage(result);
const p=`Use case: style-transfer.
Edit target: the supplied Scrapkeep concept. Preserve its exact camera, framing, positions, fox pilot identity, sphere size, boss size and pose, dam silhouette, colors, light direction and circular attack footprint.
Change its treatment to a visibly STYLIZED PAINTED WORKSHOP MINIATURE suitable as a practical 3D game-art target. The current image is too photorealistic. Simplify the entire scene's small detail into bold sculpted forms and broad hand-painted material patches. Broad bevels, large chipped enamel shapes, deliberate rounded-cast industrial shapes, simple stylized foliage clumps, smooth sculpted fox fur rather than individual hairs, simple readable plates and joints. No photographic rock grain, tiny rust speckles, micro scratches, bark detail, film grain or focus blur. Keep glass fully transparent with only two or three restrained reflection accents so the pilot is clear. Keep rich tactile material separation and volume, not a flat cartoon; do not make pristine toys.
The route must read as a gently concave bank for rolling balls, with its far-right stone shoulder rising smoothly; retain its existing route and completely unobstructed left escape space outside the danger circle. Remove fine pavement block patterning and sharp curb lips across the route in favor of continuous worn stone. Keep the hazard circle flush on the ground as a projected visual marking, not a raised physical platform or painted architecture.
Use soft, broad lighting and stylized forms, no depth of field anywhere. All near and distant silhouettes stay sharp at their scale. No text, HUD, logos or new objects. This is one concept reference, not a game screenshot.`;
store("prompt_a1",p);
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development/sketches/core-loop/design-v2/visual-development/prompt-a1.txt\n+"+p.split("\n").join("\n+")+"\n*** End Patch"));
text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:"mkdir -p artifacts/local/visual-development/attempts; cp /home/andrew/.codex/generated_images/01a0e573-1ef4-7012-b126-a44152e43072/exec-3ec8ff49-08c5-49e6-983a-343f016ad7ce.png artifacts/local/visual-development/attempts/a0.png","workdir":"/tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development","max_output_tokens":1000}));
