const p=`Edit only TWO geometric features of the supplied stylized game concept; keep the painterly 3D rendering, palette, time of day, fox pilot, camera, relative subject scale, background dam and boss unchanged.
1. REPLACE THE FLAT PAVED BRIDGE AND CIRCULAR BOSS PLAZA. Make the immediate approach a very broad smooth shallow halfpipe carved into sandstone, a visibly concave U-shaped cross-section with a rising bank on the right. It sweeps past the LEFT SIDE of the boss as a clearly visible, ball-width-plus bypass and continues behind it toward the dam. Show the curved bank through broad simple shading. Remove all the square paving tiles, circular stone plinth and crosswise step lips around the boss. The Warden stands on the same smooth continuous stone ground, with only a projected translucent red-orange circular attack outline and a few diagonal hazard strokes inside it. This is temporary projected light on stone, NOT a painted ring road or physical platform. Show the bypass outside the circle.
2. DETACH THE COPPER/PETROL EQUATOR RING FROM THE PLAYER'S GLASS BALL. There is a clearly visible continuous gap of air between ring and glass. The ring is slightly wider than the ball but near horizontal with ground clearance. It floats via the bright mint coil beneath the seated pilot. The glass ball itself remains perfectly spherical, fully enclosing the fox. Keep its internal cradle and seams; remove any posts or straps attaching the outer ring to the glass. Do not add extra rings or change the character.
Only these geometry corrections. Preserve all established visual treatment. No text, HUD, lens blur or new entities.`;
store("prompt_a2",p);
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development/sketches/core-loop/design-v2/visual-development/prompt-a2.txt\n+"+p.split("\n").join("\n+")+"\n*** End Patch"));
