const r=await tools.image_gen__imagegen({prompt:load("prompt_a2"),referenced_image_paths:["/home/andrew/.codex/generated_images/01a0e573-1ef4-7012-b126-a44152e43072/exec-b94dbbfa-342a-4d87-b578-135500c281e4.png"]});store("image_a2_result",r);generatedImage(r);
const common=`Use case: style-transfer. Edit target: supplied Scrapkeep style A concept. Produce one 16:9 variant of EXACTLY this scene. Keep camera, framing, fox pilot's identity and posture, clear enclosing glass sphere and separated orbit ring, the banked rolling route and left bypass, boss pose and size, projected circular red-orange threat boundary, dam towers, background structures and vegetation positions identical. Keep the same light direction, afternoon time, palette and visibility. This comparison varies ART TREATMENT ONLY, not content, geography, character, gameplay or mood. Player working coil light stays mint, boss cracks blue. The sphere remains transparent and round, not a faceted opaque crystal. All near silhouettes stay clear and the escape route stays unobstructed. No labels, text, HUD, logos or new objects.`;
const b=common+`\nTREATMENT B: INDUSTRIAL ADVENTURE COMIC. Strong art-directed cel-shaded 3D graphic adventure. Two to three bold shading bands per material, selective charcoal contour lines around key hero/boss silhouettes and structural edges, controlled sparse angular ink marks for chips and grease. Warm sandstone is large clean color masses, cool sky shadows. Simplify foliage into strong leaf-cloud silhouettes and rocks into deliberate shapes. Crisp material boundaries, almost no small texture. The glass has sparse graphic white reflection arcs and transparent interior; never dense hatching over the pilot. Wear follows joints and use. Keep color saturation disciplined, not neon. No photoreal texture, no soft photographic blur, no detailed stippling, no halftone dots. The boss must look heavy and menacing through bold mass and posture. Rich spatial depth despite graphic simplification.`;
const c=common+`\nTREATMENT C: CARVED CANYON MACHINERY. Sculptural, visibly faceted stylized 3D adventure art. Broad planar sandstone surfaces, deliberate low-to-mid-poly sculpted foliage clusters, chunky forged platework and strong planar light breaks. Dry-brushed pigment in a few broad patches, no tiny surface noise. No black comic outlines and no cel bands: use continuous but restrained diffuse shading across intentional planar geometry. Angular geology and cast boss plates rhyme as forms; repaired smooth curved gyro ring and round CLEAR glass sphere create purposeful contrast. Keep the pilot's fox face and ears simplified and expressive, not realistic individual hairs. Warm sun-lit planes and cool shaded planes, atmospheric blue mountains. Clearly more geometric and sculptural than the original, but not crude triangulated decimation and not pristine plastic. Preserve tactile material separation, worn enamel and working copper.`;
store("prompt_b",b);store("prompt_c",c);
for(const [name,prompt] of [["b",b],["c",c]])text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development/sketches/core-loop/design-v2/visual-development/prompt-"+name+".txt\n+"+prompt.split("\n").join("\n+")+"\n*** End Patch"));
