const common=`Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: Scrapkeep concept atlas sheet in OWNER-SELECTED STYLE A.
The supplied image is a STYLE REFERENCE ONLY. Reuse its tactile stylized 3D painted-workshop-miniature rendering: broad bevels, chunky readable masses, broad purposeful paint chips, distinct matte stone/worn enamel/copper/rubber/clear glass, soft material transitions, clear silhouettes and atmospheric depth. Invent fresh compositions specified below; do not repeat its boss, fox, dam or camera unless requested. No photographic microdetail, pristine plastic, black comic outlines, tiny text, blur or ornamental neon. Geology, machinery and culture must explain function. Every player ball is a true clear sphere enclosing an upright visible pilot, with a repaired gimbal cradle and a separate external gyro ring. No exposed pilot or wheeled vehicle. Use concentrated mint only at working collectors, red-orange/charcoal only for hostile warnings, blue only for ancient machine seams. This is concept art, not runtime evidence.`;
store("atlas_common",common);
const defs=[
["01-regions",`Create a polished landscape concept atlas of FIVE regions, arranged as five wide horizontal panorama strips stacked vertically, each with a small clear label at its left. Give each region equally generous detail and distinctly different geology, vegetation, atmosphere and useful ball-traversable terrain. No characters necessary.
Labels and scenes:
"YARD COMMONS": Sonoran foothill repair settlement, saguaros and rocky washes, warm dusty sky, patched mobile awnings, banked stone lanes and halfpipe public square, natural landform dominates.
"SPILLWAY WORKS": vast sandstone gorge, cool green riparian river, maintained pumps following canyon edges, banked dry bypass, higher chutes and tower landmark, giant natural scale.
"IRON ORCHARD": cultivated upland green valley, fruit tree rows, irrigation and patched greenhouse, smooth broad turning aprons and low banks between cultivation, bright morning and cared-for machinery; not a forest of scrap.
"FOUNDRY CROWN": cool gray forested mountains, lower pine slopes becoming bare high ridge, compact supported forging terraces, broad banked switchbacks and cable baskets; small warm furnace light against crisp blue sky.
"PALE BASIN": vast white dry mineral dunes with cool blue shadows, sparse yucca-like plants ONLY at stable margins, a wind-driven maintenance rig and partially buried ancient ribs, smooth hard-packed route that reveals ground beyond a crest. Dry gypsum-like sand, not snow. No cactus in forests or dunes. Original scene design, no franchise references. Large landscape overview sheet with clear regional variety. These are candidate regions, not a travel route map.`,["W01","W02","W03","W04","W05","W09"]],
["02-ball-culture",`Create a SIX-PANEL 3 columns by 2 rows concept sheet, landscape format, with generous clear panel boundaries. Each panel is a detailed fresh scene, not a tiny icon. Small exact labels below each panel:
"BANKED STREETS": lived-in Southwest village for gyro balls, broad concave streets and halfpipe plaza, doorways and counters at pilot eye height, route through clear.
"PACKED / CAMP": one wheeled-free collapsible tent-and-workbench camp beside a compact packed version, reusable ribs and canvas, show how rolling nomads move home without inventing large vehicles.
"PUBLIC LAUNCH": repaired steampunk public cannon with a broad approach chute, clearly marked launch direction by physical barrel and a visible distant banked landing, no person at muzzle.
"WORKING MACHINES": a useful steam lift, a heavy flow-control valve and a ball launcher integrated in canyon terrain, readable moving parts and load paths.
"THREE TRADITIONS": three small workshop fronts at same scale, fox compact cable/winch construction, bird open trusses and tension cables, robust workshop thick forgings; coherent shared salvage technology and species culture without caricature.
"SMALL COMFORTS": intimate rest nook with repaired workbench, mugs, tin plant, glove hooks, low service shelf, broad curved floor for a sphere. Wear follows use. Whole sheet warm, rowdy, lived-in, ingenious. Natural terrain and useful routes remain generous. Tiny enclosed animal pilots in clear spheres may show scale but never exposed pilots, cars or ladders as the main circulation.`,["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06"]],
["03-pilots",`Create a THREE-COLUMN character and machinery sheet on neutral warm gray, same scale, same light, identical 3/4 front view. Small labels only: "SABLE", "RIVET", "KEST". Each column has one large main view and a smaller side and rear view below. These are three current demo pilots, each visibly seated or perched INSIDE an identical-sized true clear sphere. Sphere contacts floor, one external near-horizontal gyro ring visibly separate from glass, ring clears ground. Actual ball exterior transparent enough to read the pilot. Handbuilt internal cradle, controls and salvaged electromagnet machinery. No armored sphere that hides the pilot, no wheels, no exposed animal.
SABLE: orange fox with cream muzzle, dark work cap, practical jacket and gloves, expressive ears. Compact felt-lined seat and a rope spool/winch with readable line exit. Single copper/petrol gyro ring carries mint pips, working mint coil at bottom. Do not make whole body mint.
RIVET: stocky mole machinist, broad shovel-like forepaws on controls, visor that leaves nose visible, robust low backed seat, copper heat fins and precise laser rail. Gyro ring has copper chevrons, copper working light with shared small mint collection coil beneath.
KEST: expressive bird with crest, goggles, beak visible, feet gripping an open perch, lightweight truss cradle, mortar and amber banded explosive satchels. Gyro ring has a few restrained starburst points and amber fuse lights; amber bands are horizontal, NOT diagonal hazard tape. Shared mint intake coil remains small.
Materials worn petrol enamel, copper, bone repairs, clear glass, oily joints. Character body determines the seat and equipment; silhouette of tool tells class. No extra pilots or lore labels. Need appealing characters, practical machinery and legibility, not generic cute toys.`,["H01","H02","H03","H04","H08"]]
];
store("atlas_defs",defs);
for(const [id,p,coverage] of defs){store(id,common+"\n"+p);text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /tmp/scrapkeep-visual-development/sketches/core-loop/design-v2/visual-development/prompt-"+id+".txt\n+"+(common+"\n"+p).split("\n").join("\n+")+"\n*** End Patch"));}
